天哪。

1121
01:02:42.880 --> 01:02:43.600
My buddy.
我的伙伴。

1122
01:02:44.020 --> 01:02:44.720
We will never get.
我们永远也记不住。

1123
01:02:44.800 --> 01:02:47.860
We literally just listened to it, and it's not landing on me.
我们刚才明明听到了，但我就是记不住。

1124
01:02:47.860 --> 01:02:53.080
But here's, I can only hear big brother, kid sister, because that's what you and John did for so long on set.
但我只能听到“大哥哥，小妹妹”，因为那是你和约翰在片场说了那么久的梗。

1125
01:02:53.240 --> 01:02:55.660
But, Angela, here is what creeped me out.
但是，安吉拉，让我觉得毛骨悚然的是这个。

1126
01:02:55.700 --> 01:03:01.260
When I watched that commercial and I saw that doll, my God, it looks like you.
当我看了那个广告，看到那个娃娃时，天哪，它长得真像你。

1127
01:03:02.560 --> 01:03:03.380
Oh, come on.
哦，得了吧。

1128
01:03:03.620 --> 01:03:07.820
Lady, braid your hair and you are kid sister.
女士，你把头发编起来，你就是那个小妹妹。

1129
01:03:08.100 --> 01:03:08.600
It is.
确实是。

1130
01:03:09.560 --> 01:03:11.480
Well, John is who started it.
嗯，是约翰先开始的。

1131
01:03:11.480 --> 01:03:22.100
He said to me, he called me kid sister, and then clearly, classic Kinsey, I got it wrong, and I went, big brother, instead of my buddy.
他叫我小妹妹，然后很明显，典型的金西风格，我搞错了，我说成了“大哥哥”，而不是“我的伙伴”。

1132
01:03:22.660 --> 01:03:26.800
Well, he nailed it on kid sister because the resemblance is eerie.
嗯，他叫“小妹妹”叫得太准了，因为那相似度简直诡异。

1133
01:03:27.120 --> 01:03:30.500
Well, I guess I'm just going to have to go get one.
好吧，我想我得去买一个回来。

1134
01:03:30.660 --> 01:03:31.620
Don't get one.
别买。

1135
01:03:31.620 --> 01:03:34.820
It will scare people in your home if they come upon it.
如果有人去你家看到它，会被吓到的。

1136
01:03:35.100 --> 01:03:38.260
It'll be like you putting a Chucky doll in your house.
那就像你在家里放了个鬼娃恰吉一样。

1137
01:03:38.400 --> 01:03:39.260
You can't do it.
你不能这么做。

1138
01:03:39.260 --> 01:03:42.340
I'm going to get one, and I'm going to put it by my mailbox.
我要去买一个，然后把它放在我的邮箱旁边。

1139
01:03:43.220 --> 01:03:49.120
I thought you were going to say you were going to put it in my window or something, and I'd be like, ah, what is that right there?
我还以为你会说你要把它放在我的窗户边什么的，然后我会想，啊，那是什么鬼东西？

1140
01:03:49.120 --> 01:03:50.480
I think now I have to.
我想现在我必须得这么做了。

1141
01:03:50.660 --> 01:03:51.680
No, don't you dare.
不，你敢。

1142
01:03:52.100 --> 01:03:54.520
How do you prank someone in a pandemic?
在疫情期间怎么恶作剧别人？

1143
01:03:55.000 --> 01:03:55.800
That's how.
就是这样。

1144
01:03:56.020 --> 01:03:58.640
You get a creepy doll and set it outside their window.
你买个诡异的娃娃，放在他们窗外。

1145
01:03:58.680 --> 01:04:00.880
A creepy doll that looks just like you.
一个长得跟你一模一样的诡异娃娃。

1146
01:04:01.420 --> 01:04:01.860
Yeah.
没错。

1147
01:04:02.120 --> 01:04:07.080
All right, guys, we also got some mail that is not specific to Casino Night.
好了，伙计们，我们还收到了一些不属于《赌场之夜》的来信。

1148
01:04:07.300 --> 01:04:07.700
Okay.
好的。

1149
01:04:07.700 --> 01:04:19.700
Why do some characters on the show have character names like Pam, Jim, Roy, Dwight, and some have their real names, Oscar, Creed, Angela, Phyllis?
为什么剧中的一些角色名字是帕姆、吉姆、罗伊、德怀特，而有些角色用的是演员的真名，比如奥斯卡、克里德、安吉拉、菲利斯？

1150
01:04:19.840 --> 01:04:22.720
We get this question, I would say, the moSt.
我们收到这个问题，我敢说，是最多的。

1151
01:04:23.200 --> 01:04:24.200
In the mailbox.
在邮箱里。

1152
01:04:24.200 --> 01:04:24.980
Every single week.
每周都是如此。

1153
01:04:25.040 --> 01:04:25.180
Yeah.
没错。

1154
01:04:25.640 --> 01:04:26.440
Every single week.
每周都是如此。

1155
01:04:26.600 --> 01:04:31.240
So I feel like we have maybe answered this before, but we want to take it again.
所以我觉得我们之前可能回答过这个问题，但我们想再回答一次。

1156
01:04:31.780 --> 01:04:39.240
We answered it in one of our candy bag episodes, but we're going to answer it here because we really feel like people want to know.
我们在之前的“糖果袋”剧集里回答过，但我们打算在这里再回答一遍，因为我们真的觉得大家很想知道。

1157
01:04:39.240 --> 01:04:49.240
Well, listen, you know, we had asked Greg about this, and he said, obviously, some characters are based on characters from the original British office, right?
听着，你知道的，我们问过格雷格这个问题，他说很明显，有些角色是基于英国版《办公室》里的角色设定的，对吧？

1158
01:04:49.460 --> 01:04:51.080
Jim and Pam and Dwight.
吉姆、帕姆和德怀特。

1159
01:04:51.080 --> 01:04:55.780
And then there were these new characters, and it was myself and Oscar.
然后还有这些新角色，就是我和奥斯卡。

1160
01:04:55.900 --> 01:05:03.000
We weren't in the original, and they just used our names, and just kind of, it stuck.
我们并没有出现在原版里，他们只是用了我们的名字，然后就这么定下来了。

1161
01:05:03.000 --> 01:05:09.340
I think what's interesting, Angela, did Greg ask your permission to use your name, or did he just name you Angela?
我觉得很有趣的一点是，安吉拉，格雷格当时征求过你用真名的许可吗，还是他直接就给你取名叫安吉拉了？

1162
01:05:10.820 --> 01:05:11.420
No.
没有。

1163
01:05:11.660 --> 01:05:12.860
No one said anything.
没人跟我说过什么。

1164
01:05:13.140 --> 01:05:20.600
The only conversation I ever remember having is he asked me if I had any pitches for my last name.
我唯一记得的对话就是他问我有没有关于姓氏的建议。

1165
01:05:20.600 --> 01:05:21.360
Oh.
噢。

1166
01:05:21.660 --> 01:05:23.980
And I did pitch Martin.
我确实提议过“马丁”。

1167
01:05:24.220 --> 01:05:25.860
But this was several episodes in.
但那是拍了好几集之后的事了。

1168
01:05:25.960 --> 01:05:30.500
I was already Angela, and then we were talking about, well, what would your last name be?
当时我已经是安吉拉了，然后我们在讨论，你的姓氏会是什么呢？

1169
01:05:30.580 --> 01:05:34.800
And I wrote down a list of them, and one of them was Martin, and that cleared.
我写了一张名单，其中一个就是马丁，然后就通过了。

1170
01:05:34.940 --> 01:05:36.860
Is that significant to you in some way?
这对你有什么特别的意义吗？

1171
01:05:37.740 --> 01:05:39.780
Is Martin a family name or something?
马丁是你的家族姓氏之类的吗？

1172
01:05:40.620 --> 01:05:41.060
No.
不是。

1173
01:05:41.320 --> 01:05:42.480
I just was trying to think.
我只是试着想一想。

1174
01:05:42.580 --> 01:05:49.420
I thought it was interesting that Kevin was Kevin Malone, and Oscar was Oscar Martinez, and then I'd be Angela Martin.
我觉得很有趣的是，凯文叫凯文·马龙，奥斯卡叫奥斯卡·马丁内斯，然后我叫安吉拉·马丁。

1175
01:05:49.420 --> 01:05:50.660
And we'd be the three M's.
这样我们就是三个“M”了。

1176
01:05:50.800 --> 01:05:58.780
And then we, for years, had a running joke that our spinoff would be the accountants go have their own firm called M, M, and M.
多年来我们一直有个梗，说我们的衍生剧就是会计们去开自己的事务所，名字叫“M、M and M”。

1177
01:05:59.220 --> 01:06:00.260
I love it.
我喜欢这个主意。

1178
01:06:00.820 --> 01:06:01.880
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

1179
01:06:02.180 --> 01:06:03.520
Well, there you have it, guys.
好了，伙计们，答案就在这儿了。

1180
01:06:03.820 --> 01:06:09.380
That's why some people have their real names, and some people have character names.
这就是为什么有些人用真名，而有些人用角色名。

1181
01:06:09.560 --> 01:06:10.360
Nothing like their name.
跟他们的名字一点关系都没有。

1182
01:06:11.460 --> 01:06:11.940
Yeah.
没错。

1183
01:06:12.120 --> 01:06:15.300
I think the writers just were like, ah, we'll use their names.
我想编剧们当时只是觉得，啊，就用他们的名字吧。

1184
01:06:15.440 --> 01:06:18.880
It's really not probably that interesting of a story.
这故事可能真的没那么有趣。

1185
01:06:18.880 --> 01:06:19.760
But there you go.
但事实就是这样。

1186
01:06:20.040 --> 01:06:23.140
Guys, thank you so much for sending in your questions.
伙计们，非常感谢你们发来的问题。

1187
01:06:23.340 --> 01:06:24.620
This was so much fun.
这真的太有趣了。

1188
01:06:25.360 --> 01:06:28.440
I loved this revisited episode, Angela.
安吉拉，我很喜欢这次重温剧集。

1189
01:06:28.740 --> 01:06:34.180
Honestly, one of our favorite things that we do is get to read comments and interact with you guys.
老实说，我们最喜欢做的事情之一就是阅读评论并与你们互动。

1190
01:06:34.220 --> 01:06:36.020
And I just love that.
我真的很喜欢这一点。

1191
01:06:36.180 --> 01:06:37.200
I love The Office.
我爱《办公室》。

1192
01:06:37.400 --> 01:06:39.240
Jenna and I obviously loved this show.
珍娜和我显然都很爱这部剧。

1193
01:06:39.240 --> 01:06:47.120
So we love getting to interact with fans that also loved it and have questions and comments and things that you caught that we missed.
所以我们很喜欢与同样热爱这部剧的粉丝互动，回答你们的问题和评论，以及你们发现而我们错过的细节。

1194
01:06:47.120 --> 01:06:48.040
I love all of it.
我喜欢这一切。

1195
01:06:48.040 --> 01:06:54.560
I also really like the idea of being able to deep dive with some of, like, the original visionaries for the show.
我也很喜欢能与这部剧最初的构想者们深入探讨的想法。

1196
01:06:54.820 --> 01:06:58.000
Like, we have to get Dave Rogers, our editor.
比如，我们得请我们的剪辑师戴夫·罗杰斯来。

1197
01:06:58.340 --> 01:07:02.620
We've got to get Carrie Bennett, who designed our wardrobe season one in the beginning.
我们得请第一季初期负责服装设计的嘉莉·贝内特来。

1198
01:07:02.620 --> 01:07:05.660
And, like, Randall Einhorn, our cinematographer.
还有我们的摄影指导兰德尔·艾因霍恩。

1199
01:07:06.140 --> 01:07:06.540
Kentapedia!
肯塔百科！

1200
01:07:07.340 --> 01:07:07.740
Kentapedia!
肯塔百科！

1201
01:07:08.000 --> 01:07:08.400
Kentapedia!
肯塔百科！

1202
01:07:08.420 --> 01:07:10.120
We have to get Kentapedia.
我们得搞个肯塔百科。

1203
01:07:10.140 --> 01:07:12.640
Okay, so I don't know what we're going to call these.
好吧，我不知道我们该叫它什么。

1204
01:07:12.780 --> 01:07:15.520
But from time to time, we're going to give you, what do we want to call it, Angela?
但时不时地，我们要给你们提供一些内容，安吉拉，我们叫它什么好呢？

1205
01:07:15.660 --> 01:07:16.420
A deep dive?
深度挖掘？

1206
01:07:16.580 --> 01:07:17.380
A revisited?
重温系列？

1207
01:07:17.580 --> 01:07:18.740
We'll figure it out.
我们再想想。

1208
01:07:18.880 --> 01:07:20.540
You guys actually tell us.
你们来告诉我们吧。

1209
01:07:20.540 --> 01:07:26.200
If we do an episode like this again, should we call it the deep dive or the revisited?
如果我们再做一期这样的节目，我们应该叫它“深度挖掘”还是“重温系列”？

1210
01:07:26.200 --> 01:07:27.500
I like the deep dive.
我喜欢“深度挖掘”。

1211
01:07:27.700 --> 01:07:30.820
Well, I mean, you got a deep, you got a dive.
嗯，我是说，你有“深度”，也有“挖掘”。

1212
01:07:30.980 --> 01:07:32.980
You put them together, get a deep dive.
合在一起，就是“深度挖掘”。

1213
01:07:33.160 --> 01:07:33.360
No.
不。

1214
01:07:33.880 --> 01:07:34.100
No.
不。

1215
01:07:34.440 --> 01:07:35.960
That's my son did that.
那是我儿子说的。

1216
01:07:36.160 --> 01:07:36.880
My son.
我儿子。

1217
01:07:37.380 --> 01:07:39.780
That's my son, Angela.
那是我儿子，安吉拉。

1218
01:07:40.700 --> 01:07:42.120
And you're like, no.
而你却说，不。

1219
01:07:42.780 --> 01:07:43.260
No.
不。

1220
01:07:44.540 --> 01:07:46.080
That is horrible.
那太糟糕了。

1221
01:07:46.540 --> 01:07:47.100
No, I'm kidding.
不，我开玩笑的。

1222
01:07:49.060 --> 01:07:50.060
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1223
01:07:50.140 --> 01:07:50.540
Hilarious.
太搞笑了。

1224
01:07:50.720 --> 01:07:50.900
Okay.
好吧。

1225
01:07:51.040 --> 01:07:53.260
Okay, so, guys, keep sending in your questions.
好了，各位，请继续发送你们的问题。

1226
01:07:53.260 --> 01:07:57.760
We have folders over on officeladies.com to submit questions for specific episodes.
我们在 officeladies.com 上有专门的文件夹，可以提交针对特定剧集的问题。

1227
01:07:58.000 --> 01:08:02.520
You can also send us an email at officeladies at earwolf.com.
你们也可以发邮件到 officeladies@earwolf.com。

1228
01:08:03.440 --> 01:08:06.020
Yes, we love engaging with you on our social media.
是的，我们很喜欢在社交媒体上与你们互动。

1229
01:08:06.240 --> 01:08:09.740
You can follow us over at officeladiespod on Instagram.
你们可以在 Instagram 上关注我们的账号 officeladiespod。

1230
01:08:09.920 --> 01:08:12.340
And thank you so much to Ken Kwapis.
非常感谢肯·卡皮斯。

1231
01:08:12.340 --> 01:08:15.240
And thank you guys so much for listening in.
也非常感谢大家的收听。

1232
01:08:15.500 --> 01:08:17.260
Yeah, we'll be back next week with The Merger.
是的，下周我们将带着《合并》那一集回来。

1233
01:08:19.060 --> 01:08:21.060
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

1234
01:08:21.340 --> 01:08:24.820
